            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Life</strong><br>\nJung was known for his introspective persona, using his life experiences, including visions and dreams, as research for his theories. He married Emma Rauschenbach in 1903, and they had five children.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Writings and Publications</strong><br>\nJung was a prolific writer; his collected works include significant texts such as \"Psychology and Alchemy,\" \"Psychological Types,\" and \"Man and His Symbols.\" His writings reflect his vast knowledge of the human psyche and his lifelong effort to understand it.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nJung's contribution to psychology is monumental, providing a rich, alternative view of the human mind. His concepts of introversion and extraversion, as well as synchronicity, have had a lasting impact on the understanding of human behavior.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
